<item>
  <title>Interactive volcano plots in JavaScript with CanvasXpress</title>
  <dc:creator>Isaac Neuhaus</dc:creator>
  <link>https://neuhausi.github.io/canvasxpress-blog/posts/js/volcano-plots-in-javascript/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<p>A volcano plot puts log fold change on x, statistical significance on y, and pushes the interesting genes into the top corners. CanvasXpress is a <strong>JavaScript</strong> library at heart, so in the browser there’s no wrapper at all — you give a <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code> a <code>data</code> object and a <code>config</code>, and you get an interactive, reproducible figure. The same spec renders identically from R and Python too.</p>
<section id="load-the-library" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="load-the-library">Load the library</h2>
